GDCE-I -- Graph Diffusion Counterfactual Explanation via Inversion
==================================================================

This repository is a derivative work.

1. DiGress
----------
The diffusion model, the graph transformer, the dataset abstractions, the
molecular metrics and the orca helper come from DiGress:

    Vignac, Krawczuk, Siraudin, Wang, Cevher, Frossard,
    "DiGress: Discrete Denoising Diffusion for Graph Generation", ICLR 2023
    https://github.com/cvignac/DiGress            (MIT)

The MIT licence of DiGress is reproduced in LICENSE, with its original
copyright line intact.  Files that are substantially unchanged from DiGress
include src/models/transformer_model.py, src/diffusion/*, src/metrics/*,
src/datasets/abstract_dataset*.py and src/analysis/*.

2. FreeGress
------------
Classifier-free guidance for discrete graph diffusion, the guidance config
layout and the p_uncond / s machinery follow FreeGress:

    Ninniri, Podda, Bacciu,
    "Classifier-free graph diffusion for molecular property targeting",
    ECML PKDD 2024
    https://github.com/Asduffo/FreeGress

3. SA score
-----------
src/metrics/sascorer.py is the RDKit contribution of Ertl and Schuffenhauer
(BSD-3-Clause, shipped with RDKit).

4. What is new here
-------------------
The inversion of a guided discrete diffusion trajectory and everything built on
it is the contribution of this paper:

    src/diffusion/discrete_inversion.py        naive and posterior Gumbel inversion
    src/inversion_mutag_mol.py                 the per-graph budget search
    src/inversion_benzene.py
    src/inversion_nci1_nofreq.py
    src/review_paired_tau.py                   the paired fixed-budget comparison
    src/shared_judge/                           the shared-classifier protocol,
                                                the portable classifier format and
                                                the NAFR / NA metrics
    src/review_metrics.py, src/review_dump_metrics.py
    analysis/                                   the table-producing scripts

5. Baselines
------------
No upstream baseline repository is redistributed here.  baselines/<name>/
carries the upstream URL, the pinned commit, a patch against it and our own
adapter files; baselines/setup_baselines.sh reassembles a working checkout.  Two
of the five upstream repositories carry no licence at all, which is why this is
a patch and not a copy:

    C2Explainer    github.com/kano5266/C2Explainer                86f3e8c  MIT
    CF2 (gnn_cff)  github.com/chrisjtan/gnn_cff                   9020e74  no licence
    D4Explainer    github.com/Graph-and-Geometric-Learning/...    997b4c7  MIT
    UCExplainer    github.com/flaat/COMBINEX                      707aa65  MIT
    XPlore         on GRETEL, github.com/MarioTheOne/GRETEL       fa60bd2  GRETEL MIT,
                                                                           XPlore none

Two exceptions to "our own adapter files", both declared in the repository:

  * baselines/D4Explainer/adapter/main.py extends upstream's main.py (MIT).
    Every such file is listed in baselines/<name>/adapter-provenance.txt.
  * XPlore's own algorithm and GRETEL v2's two instance classes are NOT here.
    XPlore carries no licence, so baselines/XPlore/adapter/src/wrappers/xplore/
    ships only our framework.py plus FETCH.md, which is the exact recipe for
    rebuilding the four missing files from their sources.

6. Datasets
-----------
Mutagenicity, PROTEINS and TWITTER-Real-Graph-Partial are downloaded from the
TUDataset collection (Morris et al., 2020).  Benzene comes from Agarwal et al.,
"Evaluating explainability for graph neural networks" (2023).  None of the raw
data is redistributed here; data/README.md says how it is fetched and what the
preprocessing does.
